  "question": {
    "text": "During \" S \" estimation, 160 mg of an organic compound gives 466 mg of barium sulphate. The percentage of Sulphur in the given compound is _______ %.\n(Given molar mass in $\\mathrm{g} \\mathrm{mol}^{-1}$ of $\\mathrm{Ba}: 137, \\mathrm{~S}: 32, \\overline{\\mathrm{O}: 16}$ )",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "40",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{m} \\text { mole of } \\mathrm{BaSO}_4=\\text { mmoles of } \\mathrm{S}=\\frac{466}{233} \\\\ & \\text { Mass of } \\mathrm{S}=\\frac{466}{233} \\times 32 \\mathrm{mg} \\\\ & =64 \\mathrm{mg} \\\\ & \\% \\mathrm{~S}=\\frac{64}{160} \\times 100=40 \\%\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
